00:29:48.599 --> 00:29:51.130
driving a Leaf, and at a certain moment in
time he stopped

00:29:51.130 --> 00:29:53.959
a moment in time she said, okay, I need to
charge the car.

00:29:53.959 --> 00:29:57.912
I said, well, it's interesting, let's go
to the charging station, and at

00:29:57.912 --> 00:30:01.367
that moment there were only two charging
station on the, on the campus.

00:30:01.367 --> 00:30:03.769
But, both were occupied.

00:30:03.769 --> 00:30:06.342
So, I said so what what you do now?

00:30:06.342 --> 00:30:08.847
I said well I can't drive the car I need

00:30:08.847 --> 00:30:11.911
to wait for the these two cars to be
removed so.

00:30:11.911 --> 00:30:16.310
It we've seen the charging system is a
real concern before

00:30:16.310 --> 00:30:20.452
we see it take off of, of the sales, but
it's coming.

00:30:20.452 --> 00:30:23.689
It's coming because lot of cities, lots of
states are investing.

00:30:23.689 --> 00:30:25.650
Some only in the United States.

00:30:25.650 --> 00:30:30.685
But France, Japan, China, we are signing

00:30:30.685 --> 00:30:35.348
an agreement with cities with different
cities now.

00:30:35.348 --> 00:30:36.123
It's coming.

00:30:36.123 --> 00:30:37.537
I have zero doubt, Tony.

00:30:37.537 --> 00:30:41.876
It's much slower than we thought, but it's
not slow, because the technology

00:30:41.876 --> 00:30:44.207
is not ready, it's slow mainly, because

00:30:44.207 --> 00:30:46.817
the infrastructure is not moving fast
enough.

00:30:46.817 --> 00:30:50.915
&gt;&gt; You were here visiting the engineering
school in May, to talk about autonomous

00:30:50.915 --> 00:30:53.179
vehicles, can you just share your thoughts

00:30:53.179 --> 00:30:56.130
about why your, so excited about
autonomous vehicles?

00:30:56.130 --> 00:30:58.430
&gt;&gt; Well, autonomous vehicle, because in
fact we are moving

00:30:58.430 --> 00:31:02.110
from a period of time where the car is a
slave.

00:31:02.110 --> 00:31:06.836
You, know you break you start, to a
partner.

00:31:06.836 --> 00:31:09.899
Now he's giving you information, adding
that to what you

00:31:09.899 --> 00:31:12.662
want, and we have the pieces of technology
to do it.

00:31:12.662 --> 00:31:16.922
What does it mean, the car is your,is your
partner.

00:31:16.922 --> 00:31:20.008
For example today we have the devices in
which you get to the

00:31:20.008 --> 00:31:23.870
car, the car can measure your temperature,
it can define what's your mood.

00:31:25.650 --> 00:31:29.718
It can switch the music you, adapted to
you function of

00:31:29.718 --> 00:31:35.290
excited your angry your frustrated you're
happy it can lower the

00:31:35.290 --> 00:31:40.067
temperature into the car, or or heighten
it, it can detect

00:31:40.067 --> 00:31:43.622
an accident one or two miles in front of
you and.

00:31:43.622 --> 00:31:47.700
Change the lane or slow the temperature,
or re route, re route you.

00:31:47.700 --> 00:31:51.540
There are a lot of things when the car can
become your partner.

00:31:51.540 --> 00:31:53.767
I mean you don't have to decide, it will
decide for you.

00:31:53.767 --> 00:31:57.460
As long as you have preprograming for it.

00:31:57.460 --> 00:32:02.420
Why I think autonomous driving is going to
be a big thing for the car industry.

00:32:02.420 --> 00:32:03.960
A lot of objective reason.

00:32:03.960 --> 00:32:09.210
The first one is we want zero accident.

00:32:10.530 --> 00:32:12.540
Any car company would like zero accident.

00:32:12.540 --> 00:32:15.820
The only way you move to zero accident is

00:32:15.820 --> 00:32:20.300
autonomous driving, because 95% of
accidents happen on the street.

00:32:20.300 --> 00:32:21.834
Are human mistake.

00:32:21.834 --> 00:32:24.017
If you had make too many mistake, you made
it past you.

00:32:24.017 --> 00:32:27.500
That's number one.

00:32:27.500 --> 00:32:35.618
Number two, a baby born today has 3% of
probably living to be 100 years.

00:32:35.618 --> 00:32:39.690
A lot of people lose their driving license
at 75, 70, 80 years old.

00:32:39.690 --> 00:32:44.963
So, if you can imagine the big part of the
world population, moving toward 100 years

00:32:44.963 --> 00:32:47.814
old, and you start losing your driving
license

00:32:47.814 --> 00:32:50.609
at 70, 75 years old, you have a problem.

00:32:50.609 --> 00:32:51.187
Because the last one years are

00:32:51.187 --> 00:32:52.330
gonna be difficult without autonomous
transportation.

00:32:54.860 --> 00:32:57.580
The only way you're gonna solve it is
autonomous driving, because

00:32:57.580 --> 00:33:00.490
autonomous driving you can be handicapped,
you can have a lot

00:33:00.490 --> 00:33:04.450
of physical problem impairment and you can
still get into the

00:33:04.450 --> 00:33:09.307
car, input the address and the car will,
will drive you there.

00:33:09.307 --> 00:33:12.637
So, for me, it's in need, in term of
safety, it's

00:33:12.637 --> 00:33:18.722
a need, in term of expansion, of
autonomous, of autonomous, transportation.

00:33:18.722 --> 00:33:22.304
It's good for us, because it's an
expansion of our market, but

00:33:22.304 --> 00:33:27.076
also, it's gonna be an essential element
for, for senior, for senior people.

00:33:27.076 --> 00:33:28.250
And the pieces of technology are ready.

00:33:29.540 --> 00:33:32.660
We, we have the different technologies
that allow us.

00:33:32.660 --> 00:33:36.080
Our estimate is today, we have already
announced officially that autonomous

00:33:36.080 --> 00:33:39.780
driving will take place as mass market of
cars by 2020.

00:33:39.780 --> 00:33:41.670
We have already authorization in Japan.

00:33:41.670 --> 00:33:44.729
And I know that we have, there some
authorization in

00:33:44.729 --> 00:33:49.123
the Unites States to allow autonomous
driving testing, on the road.

00:33:49.123 --> 00:33:53.746
&gt;&gt; So my last question before I open the,
open it up to the floor for, for Q&amp;A.

